# github.com links with ANY subpath (blob/*, issues/*, pull/*, ...) against a
# public repo cannot be verified by lychee here, merge or no merge: lychee
# 0.24.2's GitHub API fallback only ever queries GET /repos/{owner}/{repo} -
# the bare root (lychee-lib/src/checker/website.rs:351-366) - so a subpath
# request runs unauthenticated against github.com's own web frontend
# regardless of GITHUB_TOKEN, and 404s or throttles independent of whether the
# target exists. Each entry below is witnessed elsewhere instead; see the
# comment naming its replacement check.

# This repo's own root files. bin/verify-excluded-links.py checks these
# against the local checkout - a stronger witness than a remote API call,
# since the CI job already holds the exact commit under test on disk.
https://github\.com/ardent-tools/ardent-tools-site/blob/main/AI-USE-POLICY\.md
https://github\.com/ardent-tools/ardent-tools-site/blob/main/LICENSE
https://github\.com/ardent-tools/ardent-tools-site/blob/main/LICENSE-DOCS

# content/systems/akroasis.md's self-filed CI gap. Cross-repo fact this repo
# cannot hold locally - witnessed by bin/verify-excluded-links.py against
# GET /repos/forkwright/akroasis/issues/262 with GITHUB_TOKEN.
https://github\.com/forkwright/akroasis/issues/262

